 4. 🐈 1 science thing: New cat dropped 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Fernando Faciole/National Geographic via Reuters Meet Leopardus tilcayo — the first newly identified cat species in over a century, according to a new study .

 The wild cat, a bit smaller than a housecat, lives in Bolivia's cloud forest. Locals call it simply "Tilcayo." 🌲 National Geographic on the discovery's importance: "The new paper doesn't just name a new species; it redraws the cat family tree to have a lot more branches than previously thought."

 "What's more, the researchers hope the methods used to identify L. tilcayo may soon be used to find even more cat species spread across the world, and even transform how we protect them." Go deeper ... Read the study . 

 
 
